   "k": "62jnd2",
   "en": "Strategies and Guides"
  },
  {
   "k": "1345498",
   "en": "The below is ⟦0⟧ player suggested strategies for ⟦1⟧. Bear in mind, due to the dynamic nature of the game, it may unfold differently for other players.",
   "frags": 2
  },
  {
   "k": "sabr76",
   "en": "Bunkerburg"
  },
  {
   "k": "tdubq0",
   "en": "There is little hope for Luxembourg to survive in the face of her powerful neighbors: the ⟦0⟧, in particular, almost always use a focus to declare war on the BeNeLux to go around the Maginot line. Nevertheless, Luxembourg can greatly extend her existence by constructing land forts on its only province since day one. These forts, protected from being encircled and cut off from the capital, will end up more useful than the entire Maginot Line. Entrench as deep as possible, focus on defensive divisions, add a few artillery battalions, expand your army to no more than wide enough for the entire border (240), and try to cause as much casualties to your enemies as possible.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "i87c38",
   "en": "German Reich"
  },
  {
   "k": "qlvjj7",
   "en": "Generally, since you only have 8 Iron and no fuel (and no way to buy resources, since you have no factories ⟦0⟧), using motorized/mechanized units or aircraft would be hard. Due to lack of resources and industry, amount of equipment produced will be small. You will heavily rely on lend-lease - what should help with basic things, and even get something interesting and high-tech on occasions (e.g. artillery, mechanized units, armored cars, tanks, aircraft, etc).",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "dpxmj7",
   "en": "and are about to be encircled with Axis"
  },
  {
   "k": "11602ln",
   "en": "Once you max out land forts, consider building Anti-Air to decrease efficiency of enemy aviation. Air Base isn't very useful - lend-leased aircraft are acquired in small numbers, Axis will just shoot all of them down. Radar is unneeded. Factories and infrastructure are OK after finishing forts. Synthetic Refinery could make fuel for lend-leased vehicles - but that's only useful ⟦0⟧ you get vehicles via lend-lease in the first place.",
   "frags": 1
  },
  {
   "k": "ozmp5y",
   "en": "Join Axis"
  },
  {
   "k": "haufv5",
   "en": "Another strategy for Luxembourg and her hope for survival is to become fascist and join the axis. When Germany invades France or Belgium, Luxembourg (as an ally of Germany) can send in what little troops she has, and can attempt to assist enough in order to gain enough war experience, and potentially take some counties in Belgium, maybe even in France as well. From there, it gets a little easier, as with more land come more factories, which will help her industry. Don't bother with naval, or even aerial research for that matter, as in the early stages it isn't that necessary, however, a good boost to the army would be paratroopers, researching paratroopers will make it easier to annex the Netherlands, and Belgium if the German Reich hasn't attacked yet. Even if an initial attack fails on Belgium and Holland, if Luxembourg is an ally of Germany, she can call the Germans in to assist and win the war."
  },
